  "content_body": "Nursing & Feeding\n\nMaternity\n\nNursing & Feeding\n\nBaby Carriers\n\nNursery\n\nCar Seats\n\nBaby Monitors\n\nStrollers\n\nDiapering Essentials\n\nToys\n\nFeeding your baby can come with challenges, whether you’re breastfeeding, bottle feeding or doing a combination of the two. Fortunately, there are a wide range of products that can help eliminate (most of) the feeding frenzy and make mealtime a little more enjoyable for you and baby. Here, you’ll find our guides to the best breastfeeding, pumping, and bottle feeding gear, along with some helpful tips for dealing with a hangry baby.\n\nIn This Section\n\nBreastfeeding Essentials\n\nBreastfeeding seems simple enough: Baby, meet breast. But as moms who's done it will tell you, a few nursing essentials can make a big difference.\n\nBottle Feeding Essentials\n\nWhether you're exclusively bottle-feeding, supplementing with formula or pumped breastmilk, or making the switch from breast to bottle, here's what you'll need to establish a healthy bottle-feeding routine.\n\nFormula Feeding\n\nPumping Essentials\n\nNursing Bras\n\nHigh Chairs and Booster Seats\n\nStarting Solids\n\nSippy Cups\n\nThe educational health content on What To Expect is reviewed by our medical review board and team of experts to be up-to-date and in line with the latest evidence-based medical information and accepted health guidelines, including the medically reviewed What to Expect books by Heidi Murkoff. This educational content is not medical or diagnostic advice. Use of this site is subject to our terms of use and privacy policy. © 2005-2026 Everyday Health, Inc., a Ziff Davis company.\n\nOpens a new window",
